## Why This Is Asked
Tests automated incident response playbooks for cross-region database replication failures and data integrity under pressure. Emphasizes signal quality, containment, sequencing, rollback, and validation.

## Key Concepts
- Incident response runbooks across AWS accounts and regions
- DynamoDB Global Tables consistency, point-in-time recovery, and backups
- Event-driven automation with EventBridge and Step Functions
- Safe containment with SSM Automation and IAM boundaries
- Testing via controlled chaos experiments and audit trails

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Comment": "DR workflow for DynamoDB Global Tables replication failure",
  "StartAt": "DetectReplicationLag",
  "States": {
    "DetectReplicationLag": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "check-dynamodb-replication"
      },
      "Next": "ContainIncident"
    },
    "ContainIncident": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::aws-sdk:ssm:startAutomationExecution",
      "Parameters": {
        "DocumentName": "isolate-dynamodb-region"
      },
      "Next": "ValidateDataIntegrity"
    },
    "ValidateDataIntegrity": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [
        {
          "Variable": "$.validationResult",
          "StringEquals": "PASS",
          "Next": "FailoverToHealthyRegion"
        }
      ],
      "Default": "RollbackAndAlert"
    }
  }
}
```

